     mmaapp--mmbboonnee — Multicast connection mapper

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     mmaapp--mmbboonnee [--ffggnn] [--dd[_l_e_v_e_l]] [--rr _c_o_u_n_t] [--tt _s_e_c_o_n_d_s] [_s_t_a_r_t_i_n_g___r_o_u_t_e_r]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     mmaapp--mmbboonnee attempts to display all multicast routers that are reachable
     from the multicast router _s_t_a_r_t_i_n_g___r_o_u_t_e_r.  If not specified on the com‐
     mand line, _s_t_a_r_t_i_n_g___r_o_u_t_e_r is “localhost”.  mmaapp--mmbboonnee must be run as
     root.

     mmaapp--mmbboonnee sends an ASK_NEIGHBORS IGMP message to _s_t_a_r_t_i_n_g___r_o_u_t_e_r.  A re‐
     sponse contains the multicast version number of _s_t_a_r_t_i_n_g___r_o_u_t_e_r and the
     addresses of all its neighboring multicast routers.  If the multicast
     version number is recent, then mmaapp--mmbboonnee requests additional information
     such as metrics, thresholds, and flags.

     If a recursive search has been requested (see --ff), mmaapp--mmbboonnee repeats the
     above operation for each new multicast router in the list of neighbors
     and continues the process until no new multicast routers are reported.

     The options are as follows:

     --dd[_l_e_v_e_l]   Sets the debug level to _l_e_v_e_l.  When the debug level is
                 greater than the default value of 0, additional debugging
                 messages are printed to stderr.  Regardless of the debug
                 level, an error condition will always write an error message
                 and will cause mmaapp--mmbboonnee to terminate.  Non-zero debug levels
                 are:

                       1.   Print packet warnings, plus level 0 messages.

                       2.   Print notifications of down networks, plus level 1
                            messages.

                       3.   Print notifications of all packet timeouts, plus
                            level 2 messages.

                 Default is 0.

     --ff          Causes a recursive (flooding) search.  If no _s_t_a_r_t_i_n_g___r_o_u_t_e_r
                 is specified, a recursive search is always performed.

     --gg          Sets graphing format to GraphEd format.

     --nn          Disables DNS lookup for the names of the multicast routers.

     --rr _c_o_u_n_t    Sets the neighbor query retry limit to _c_o_u_n_t.  Default is 1.

     --tt _s_e_c_o_n_d_s  Sets the number of seconds to wait for a neighbor query reply
                 before retrying to _s_e_c_o_n_d_s.  Default is 2.

